{"format":1,"seq":946,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_bdrk_018b9tsQftbq6D5KFGkEFdzM","toolName":"typescript","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    \"src/functions/commands/gh.ts\",\n    \"src/functions/globals/gh.ts\",\n    \"src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts\",\n    \"test/functions/globals-integration.test.ts\",\n    \"test/globals/gh.test.ts\",\n    \"test/sandbox/run.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"pr\": \"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/382\\n\"\n}"}],"details":{"value":{"files":["src/functions/commands/gh.ts","src/functions/globals/gh.ts","src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts","test/functions/globals-integration.test.ts","test/globals/gh.test.ts","test/sandbox/run.test.ts"],"pr":"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/382\n"},"truncated":false,"functions":[{"action":"run","name":"delivery.listChangedFiles","scope":"project"},{"action":"run","name":"delivery.commit","scope":"project"}],"progress":[{"id":1,"traceSequence":2,"command":"git \"status\" \"--porcelain=v1\" \"-z\" \"--untracked-files=all\"","status":"done","output":" M src/functions/commands/gh.ts M src/functions/globals/gh.ts M src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts M test/functions/globals-integration.test.ts M test/globals/gh.test.ts M test/sandbox/run.test.ts","code":0},{"id":2,"traceSequence":4,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"diff\" \"--cached\" \"--name-only\" \"--no-renames\" \"-z\"","status":"done","output":"","code":0},{"id":3,"traceSequence":5,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"ls-files\" \"-z\" \"--\" \"src/functions/commands/gh.ts\" \"src/functions/globals/gh.ts\" \"src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts\" \"test/functions/globals-integration.test.ts\" \"test/globals/gh.test.ts\" \"test/sandbox/run.test.ts\"","status":"done","output":"src/functions/commands/gh.tssrc/functions/globals/gh.tssrc/sandbox/injection-hints.tstest/functions/globals-integration.test.tstest/globals/gh.test.tstest/sandbox/run.test.ts","code":0},{"id":4,"traceSequence":6,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"add\" \"-u\" \"--\" \"src/functions/commands/gh.ts\" \"src/functions/globals/gh.ts\" \"src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts\" \"test/functions/globals-integration.test.ts\" \"test/globals/gh.test.ts\" \"test/sandbox/run.test.ts\"","status":"done","output":"","code":0},{"id":5,"traceSequence":7,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"diff\" \"--cached\" \"--name-only\" \"--no-renames\" \"-z\"","status":"done","output":"src/functions/commands/gh.tssrc/functions/globals/gh.tssrc/sandbox/injection-hints.tstest/functions/globals-integration.test.tstest/globals/gh.test.tstest/sandbox/run.test.ts","code":0},{"id":6,"traceSequence":8,"command":"git \"commit\" \"-m\" \"fix(gh): return whole gh.api responses and name cut-short methods\\n\\n- gh.api captures up to 4 MB (the program-data budget) by default, so JSON responses parse;\\n  the 50 KB tool-output default cut them mid-document\\n- gh.api explains process options passed where its flag array belongs\\n- injection hints list the methods that extend a cut-short name (gh.pr -> gh.prCreate, ...)\\n  first, ahead of near misses in other namespaces\\n\\nRefs #379\"","status":"done","output":"[fix/gh-api-json-capture 26b3795] fix(gh): return whole gh.api responses and name cut-short methods\n 6 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n","code":0},{"id":7,"traceSequence":9,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\" \"--abbrev-ref\" \"HEAD\"","status":"done","output":"26b3795e33e70be14dbfcc5ff1c51042a149467e\nfix/gh-api-json-capture\n","code":0},{"id":8,"traceSequence":10,"command":"git \"push\" \"-u\" \"origin\" \"fix/gh-api-json-capture\"","status":"done","output":"remote: \nremote: Create a pull request for 'fix/gh-api-json-capture' on GitHub by visiting:        \nremote:      https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/new/fix/gh-api-json-capture        \nremote: \nTo https://github.com/cv/pit\n * [new branch]      fix/gh-api-json-capture -> fix/gh-api-json-capture\nbranch 'fix/gh-api-json-capture' set up to track 'origin/fix/gh-api-json-capture'.\n","code":0},{"id":9,"traceSequence":11,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"create\" \"--title\" \"fix(gh): return whole gh.api responses and name cut-short methods\" \"--body\" \"Refs #379 (area: `gh` globals and injection hints).\\n\\n**gh.api truncated JSON (5 failed calls, plus a regex workaround).** `gh.api` used the default 50 KB stream budget, so larger responses (`compare`, `pulls?per_page=4`) were cut mid-document and `JSON.parse(r.stdout)` failed with `unexpected token: 'web'` and similar (372#6, 375#5, 376#2, 376#6, 376#7). `runtime.completedCalls` returned the same cut-off value, so the suggested recovery didn't help. I reproduced it: the compare of `v2.5.1...v2.5.2` gave 50,944 bytes with `truncated: true`. Now `gh.api` defaults to the program-data budget (4 MB, 1,000,000 lines); a caller's `maxBytes`/`maxLines` still win.\\n\\n**gh.api misplaced options (375#21).** `api(endpoint, { method, fields })` failed with a bare `args must be an array of strings`. The error now gives a flag example and says that process options go in the third argument.\\n\\n**`gh.pr` guesses (370#8, 372#43, 375#6).** The hint said `Did you mean: pr, ci, gh?`, which pointed at the project `pr` namespace. Methods whose names start with the missing name now come first, both in `Did you mean` and in the bounded `gh has:` listing, so `gh.pr` points at `prCreate`, `prList`, `prMerge`, and `prView`.\\n\\nTests: `gh.api` default and override budgets, the misplaced-options error, and the cut-short-method hint. The session-override test now asserts that the caller's option reaches `execFile`, not the exact options object. `npm run check` and the test suite pass (`delivery.validate`).\" \"--base\" \"main\" \"--head\" \"fix/gh-api-json-capture\"","status":"done","output":"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/382\n","code":0}],"traces":[{"id":1,"sequence":1,"namespace":"__pit","method":"savedFunctionRun","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":